# Every line here hides a link the checker would otherwise report. Keep the list
# short, exclude URLs rather than whole hosts, and say why — a host-wide rule hides
# tomorrow's broken link as well as today's.

# Dead: Trustwave removed the custodianship announcement. The URL stays in the 2024
# blog post as the citation of what was announced at the time, and OWASP's own
# project page still carries the same dead link.
^https://www\.trustwave\.com/en-us/resources/blogs/spiderlabs-blog/trustwave-transfers-modsecurity-custodianship

# Dead: the reporter's repository cited by CVE-2024-46292 no longer exists. Kept as
# a record of what the CVE pointed at.
^https://github\.com/yoloflz101/

# 403 to every unauthenticated request. Slack refuses non-browser clients outright,
# so no URL on this workspace can be checked at all — this is not a link that might
# break, it is a host that cannot be verified. Excluded as a host rather than per
# channel, because a per-path rule would only move the same failure to the next
# channel link someone adds.
^https://owasp\.slack\.com

# 999 "Unknown status code" — LinkedIn's anti-bot response, returned to anything
# that is not a signed-in browser. Both spellings appear in the team page, and the
# profiles resolve fine by hand; CI cannot confirm that.
^https://(www\.)?linkedin\.com/
